Where the energy goes (base case)
  rereading the context               19%
  calls above 200,000 cached tokens   0%

fixed-context
  Each call re-read on average 12,600 tokens its session started with: the
  system prompt, tool definitions, instruction files and first prompt. That
  used 99% of the energy.
  What you can do:
    codex:
      enabled = false in config.toml for MCP servers you do not use
      shorten AGENTS.md
  To see the effect, run this after the change:
  `tokendraw findings --since <tomorrow>`

model-choice
  Subagents and headless runs on models pricier than gpt-6-luna (codex) used
  100% of the energy. On those models, the same tokens would have made the
  total 80% lower.
  What you can do:
    codex:
      agents.default_subagent_model = "gpt-6-luna" in config.toml
      codex exec --model gpt-6-luna
  To see the effect, run this after the change:
  `tokendraw findings --since <tomorrow>`
